		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: Defining a Kinematic Object]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=41513#p41513"><![CDATA[
It is recommended to use a fixed constraint and move the parent location of the fixed constraint. (Kinematic bodies are not supported in PyBullet)<div class="codebox"><p>Code: </p><pre><code>relativeChildPosition=[0,0,1]relativeChildOrientation=[0,0,0,1]hand_cid = p.createConstraint(hand,-1,-1,-1,p.JOINT_FIXED,[0,0,0],[0,0,0],relativeChildPosition,relativeChildOrientation)</code></pre></div>Then change the position like this:<div class="codebox"><p>Code: </p><pre><code>p.changeConstraint(hand_cid,updatedChildPosition,updatedChildOrientation)</code></pre></div>(optionally provide the maxForce=... in the changeConstraint to limit the maximum force by the fixed constraint.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2">Erwin Coumans</a> — Mon Oct 15, 2018 11:03 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
